{"n": 944, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "944.webp", "text": "ot,\n\n30 51802\n\n51-317\n\nGulde traverse of knife parallel to win-\ndow.\n\nCut through cement bead as close as\npossible to window glass.\n\n1 Body opening\n2 Cement bead\n3 Knife\n\n4 Window glass\n\nlf applicable, resharpen the knife* while\nelectric tool Is running.\n\nLift out window with Special Too!\n513010.\n\n* Source of Supply: HWB\n\n351187\n\n3051805\n\nReduce thickness of residual cement\non body opening surface to about 0.5\nmm (0.020\").\n\nCut off residual cement with universal\nknife (sharp as a razor blade) carefully,\nto avold damaging the paint finish on\nbody opening surface.\n\nImportant!\n\nAlways repair damaged paint finish to\nguarantee longterm corrosion Inhibi-\ntion!\n\nUse BMW EP filler (2K) for this pur-\n\npose.\nRemove residual cement, sand out and\ntouch up scratches In non-visible sur-\nfaces with BMW EP filler.\n\nLarge-surface damage must be sanded\ndown to blank metal and coated with\nBMW EP filler (30 ... 40 um thick coat).\nif complete paint bulidup Is necessary\non visiblé surface, prime coated ce-\nment flange must be removed prior to\napplication of fina! paint coat.\n\nReduce the residual cement to about\n0.5 mm (0.020\") when reusing the win-\ndow.\n\nBrush In window and body In area of\ncement surface with a primer (repair\nkit\").\n\nimportant!\n\nRepaired paint finish spots must be\nhardened. Only apply grimer in area of\ncement surface, singe’otherwise win-\ndow glass will be hpaired per-\nmanently.\n\nNote:\nAir drying time: at least 10 minutes.\n\n* Source of Supply: HWB", "words": [["ot,", 0.1494, 0.0577, 0.2452, 0.1001], ["30", 0.2001, 0.2686, 0.2107, 0.2772], ["51802", 0.2148, 0.2679, 0.2442, 0.2765], ["51-317", 0.4605, 0.0245, 0.5279, 0.0484], ["Gulde", 0.272, 0.0836, 0.3034, 0.0955], ["traverse", 0.3075, 0.0849, 0.3506, 0.0962], ["of", 0.3546, 0.0849, 0.3647, 0.0962], ["knife", 0.3688, 0.0849, 0.3941, 0.0968], ["parallel", 0.3982, 0.0855, 0.4367, 0.0